      "summaries": {
        "en": "Code Review Graph is a local-first tool that builds a persistent knowledge graph of your codebase, enabling AI coding assistants to focus only on relevant code during reviews. It uses static analysis (tree-sitter) and incremental updates to construct the graph, dramatically reducing LLM context size. Integrate via MCP or CLI for efficient, context-aware code review in large repositories, especially with Claude.",
        "zh": "Code Review Graph 是一款本地优先的代码智能工具，通过构建代码库的持久知识图谱，让 AI 编码助手在代码审查时只关注相关部分，解决大仓库中上下文过载的问题。它利用 tree-sitter 进行静态分析，并支持增量更新，从而显著减少 LLM 的上下文负担。你可以通过 MCP 或 CLI 轻松集成，特别适合大型项目的高效、上下文感知的代码审查，与 Claude 等 AI 工具配合使用，能大幅提升审查效率。",
        "es": "Code Review Graph is a local-first tool that builds a persistent knowledge graph of your codebase, enabling AI coding assistants to focus only on relevant code during reviews. It uses static analysis (tree-sitter) and incremental updates to construct the graph, dramatically reducing LLM context size. Integrate via MCP or CLI for efficient, context-aware code review in large repositories, especially with Claude.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "code-review-graph stands out for ai-coding, claude, and claude-code in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Code Review Graph is a local-first tool that builds a persistent knowledge graph of your codebase, enabling AI coding assistants to focus only on relevant code during reviews. It uses static analysis (tree-sitter) and incremental updates to construct the graph, dramatically reducing LLM context size. Integrate via MCP or CLI for efficient, context-aware code review in large repositories, especially with Claude.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/tirth8205/code-review-graph for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
