      },
      "summaries": {
        "en": "Wigolo is an open-source MCP server that gives AI coding agents local-first web capabilities—search, fetch, crawl, and research—without cloud APIs or API keys. Its key technical insight is running all operations locally, ensuring user privacy and zero cost per query. By leveraging the Model Context Protocol, it seamlessly integrates into agent workflows, enabling autonomous web research. Developers can deploy it as a standalone server or embed it in their tools for secure, cost-free web access.",
        "zh": "Wigolo 是一个开源的 MCP 服务器，专门为 AI 编程智能体提供本地优先的网页访问能力——搜索、抓取、爬取和研究，无需依赖云 API 或付费密钥。核心技术特色是全部操作在本地运行，因此查询零成本且保护隐私。基于模型上下文协议（MCP），它可以轻松接入各类智能体框架，让智能体自主进行在线调研。开发者既可将其部署为独立服务，也可集成到现有开发工具中。典型应用包括让代码助手自动查阅文档、抓取教程或对比技术方案。",
        "es": "Wigolo is an open-source MCP server that gives AI coding agents local-first web capabilities—search, fetch, crawl, and research—without cloud APIs or API keys. Its key technical insight is running all operations locally, ensuring user privacy and zero cost per query. By leveraging the Model Context Protocol, it seamlessly integrates into agent workflows, enabling autonomous web research. Developers can deploy it as a standalone server or embed it in their tools for secure, cost-free web access.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "wigolo stands out for agent, ai, and ai-agent in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Wigolo is an open-source MCP server that gives AI coding agents local-first web capabilities—search, fetch, crawl, and research—without cloud APIs or API keys. Its key technical insight is running all operations locally, ensuring user privacy and zero cost per query. By leveraging the Model Context Protocol, it seamlessly integrates into agent workflows, enabling autonomous web research. Developers can deploy it as a standalone server or embed it in their tools for secure, cost-free web access.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/KnockOutEZ/wigolo for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
